---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL, LINKEDIN_URL } from '../consts';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="Xin Liang Chia — engineer writing about LLMs and AI systems performance."
	pubDate={new Date('September 12 2026')}
>
	<p>
		Hi, I'm <strong>Xin Liang Chia</strong>. I'm an engineer focused on
		large language models and the systems that make them fast: GPUs, CUDA,
		inference serving, and everything in between. I write this blog to record
		what I learn — explaining a concept in my own words, with real numbers, is
		how I test whether I understand it.
	</p>

	<h2>Background</h2>
	<p>
		I worked for over six years as an AI engineer, building and operating
		production systems end to end: real-time computer-vision platforms
		processing 500+ concurrent camera streams on containerized microservices,
		cross-camera multi-object tracking, and LLM-based assistants using
		retrieval-augmented generation. I also optimized LLM training and inference
		for production on multi-server, multi-GPU on-premise infrastructure —
		fine-tuning, quantization, and serving.
	</p>
	<p>
		I hold an M.S. in Applied Mathematics, and I'm currently pursuing a Master
		of Electrical and Computer Engineering at Rice University.
	</p>

	<h2>Teaching</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Lecturer, Computer Vision and Intelligent Systems</strong> — Feng Chia
			University, Taichung, Taiwan (Sep 2023 – Jun 2024). Taught undergraduate
			computer vision and pattern recognition; ranked in the top 10% of the
			university's general courses.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Corporate Training Instructor</strong> — Industrial Technology
			Research Institute (ITRI), Taiwan (Aug 2025). Delivered professional
			training to industry engineers on AI-assisted system design workflows.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Skills</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Languages</strong> — Python, C/C++, CUDA, SQL, JavaScript.</li>
		<li><strong>ML &amp; LLMs</strong> — PyTorch, TensorFlow, computer vision (ViT, SAM, SLAM), multimodal LLMs, RAG.</li>
		<li><strong>LLM optimization</strong> — fine-tuning (SFT, PEFT/LoRA), quantization, knowledge distillation, distributed training, inference serving (vLLM, SGLang, TensorRT).</li>
		<li><strong>Systems &amp; cloud</strong> — Docker, Kubernetes, AWS, GCP, CI/CD, real-time systems.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>What's on this site</h2>
	<p>This site contains learning paths in 3 areas:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>AI Infrastructure</strong> — measurement, hardware capacity, networking, kernels, distributed training, and LLM serving.</li>
		<li><strong>Models & Mathematics</strong> — neural networks, statistical learning, Transformers, and modern model architectures.</li>
		<li><strong>Hardware & Co-Design</strong> — computer architecture, Arm and RISC-V, ASICs, accelerators, and efficient AI.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>Browse the <a href="/blog/">series catalog</a>. Series carry subject and level tags, with at most 30 articles.</p>

	<p>
		Every article follows the same rules: one concept at a time, concrete numbers
		over adjectives, original diagrams, and primary sources cited.
	</p>

	<p>
		Find me on <a href={GITHUB_URL} target="_blank">GitHub</a> and{' '}
		<a href={LINKEDIN_URL} target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>, or subscribe via{' '}
		<a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
